<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 8 June, from 632 to 1968.</p></header>
<div class="tih-pinned-card"><p class="tih-pinned-label">International day</p><p class="tih-pinned-title">World Oceans Day</p><p class="tih-pinned-desc">Officially recognised by the United Nations in 2008, World Oceans Day highlights the ocean's critical role in sustaining life on Earth and promotes global action to protect marine ecosystems from pollution and overexploitation.</p></div>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/medina" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/medina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">632 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,394 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Prophet Muhammad dies in Medina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Muhammad died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, by most traditions on this day. Within a generation his successors, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphs</a>, had carried <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">793 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vikings raid the monastery of Lindisfarne</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Norse raiders attacked the island monastery off Northumbria, killing monks and seizing treasure. The shock across Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> has made the raid a symbolic start of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1191 CE <span class="tih-ago">835 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard the Lionheart arrives at the siege of Acre</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> joined the crusaders besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a>, which surrendered five weeks later. He went on to win at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsuf">Arsuf</a> but never retook <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1845 CE <span class="tih-ago">181 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Jackson dies at the Hermitage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The seventh US president died at his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tennessee">Tennessee</a> plantation aged 78. Victor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> and champion of the 'common man', he also drove the forced removal of Native Americans.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1949 CE <span class="tih-ago">77 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Orwell's Nineteen Eighty-Four is published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Secker and Warburg published George Orwell's novel of a totalitarian surveillance state. Terms such as 'Big Brother' and 'doublethink' passed into everyday language.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1968 CE <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">James Earl Ray is arrested at Heathrow</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martin-luther">Martin Luther</a> King's killer was caught at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Heathrow travelling on a false Canadian passport. He pleaded guilty in 1969 and was sentenced to 99 years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li></ol>
